  "problem_statement": "A CoAP option whose value is 0 can be encoded in the shortest form, containing only the option number and no value bytes. unicoap must treat that encoding as an option with value 0 when reading it back. In particular, if such an option is present, unicoap_options_get_uint8(), unicoap_options_get_uint16(), and unicoap_options_get_uint32() must succeed and set their output value to 0. Today such retrieval does not return 0 for that encoding.",
